  "description": "Process indicator with four alarm relays and one retransmission output (voltage, current, RTD), with RS-232 or RS-485 Modbus RTU",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "Presys, DMY-2030 Light - Energy, Manual (section 5, Modbus registers and coils)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "DMY-2030 Light - Energy, Manual",
      "url": "https://www.presys.com.br/downloads/manual_1_168.pdf",
      "note": "section 5, linked in issue #389"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Section 5 lists registers 0 to 60 and coils 0 to 35. It does not say whether the numbers are the addresses sent on the wire or are numbered from 1; they are taken as the wire addresses (address_base 0, the first register is number 00). If a read is off by one, try address_base 1.",
    "The document says the connection details are in a separate communication manual. The slave address (0 to 99), baud rate (300 to 9600 bps) and parity (none, even, odd) are set in registers 19 to 21; the factory defaults are not given, so 9600 bps, no parity and slave 1 are placeholders. The optional communication module is RS-232 or RS-485.",
    "Values shown with a decimal point on the display are sent without it; the process variable has the number of decimals in register 1 and is given raw (divide by 10 to the power of that number).",
    "The document does not say which Modbus function reads the registers; they are taken as holding registers (FC03/FC06/FC16).",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
